WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.254
What reform looks like.

00:00:02.204 --> 00:00:04.397
Structural changes needed.

00:00:04.397 --> 00:00:11.534
After two hundred and fifty-two pages of documented institutional failure, this page outlines what real reform would require.

00:00:11.534 --> 00:00:13.659
Not policy tweaks.

00:00:13.659 --> 00:00:15.715
Not committee studies.

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:19.715
Structural changes to the architecture of institutional capture.

00:00:19.715 --> 00:00:24.420
Each reform addresses a specific failure documented across the investigation.

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:33.318
Each reform is also blocked by the captured system itself — because the institutions that would need to implement the reform are the institutions that benefit from the status quo.

00:00:33.318 --> 00:00:39.659
This is the paradox of captured democracy: the system that needs reform is the system that prevents reform.
